description=CeroSec puts a small Unix on the desktop computers of Knox County. Switch one on, sit down at it, and a green 60x20 terminal opens on a BIOS line and a login prompt. Behind it: files, permissions, accounts, an editor, shell scripts and cron. <LINE> <LINE>
description=Its /dev holds the doors, lights and locks of the building around it. Coax reaches the other machines in that building, a modem dials the county, a radio outlives it. <LINE> <LINE>
description=Server-authoritative and safe in multiplayer. No dependencies. Build 42 only. <LINE> <LINE>
